{#
  Cart | Quick — the cart summary.

  Rendered by neo_commerce's lazy builder in the page, and rendered again
  standalone every time the cart changes, to be swapped in over the top of
  itself.

  CONTRACT — three things the module depends on:

  1. `data-neo-cart="{{ variation }}"` on the OUTERMOST element, where it has
     two readers. Every cart refresh is a ReplaceCommand aimed at
     `[data-neo-cart="…"]`, so this attribute is how the response finds the
     summary — whether it was placed by block layout, an Alchemist slot or
     straight from twig, and however many of them are on the page. The
     module's script reads the same attribute off the page and sends the
     values it finds with every ajax request, which is how the server knows
     to build this summary and not the ones that are not here. Remove it and
     the count silently stops updating until the next full page load.

  2. `link_attributes` printed on the link. It carries the href, the
     accessible name, and the use-modal-ajax wiring that opens the cart in a
     shelf. Drop it and the cart navigates to /cart instead of opening.

  3. This markup mints no ids. One page can hold two carts (a desktop header
     and a mobile one) built from the same variation, and both are replaced by
     the same command with the same HTML — so any id here would be duplicated.
     That is why the link is named with aria-label rather than pointed at a
     count element with aria-describedby.

  The count carries aria-live="polite" so adding to the cart is announced
  without stealing focus from the product page.

  Own this file: it is copied into your theme on install and yours to restyle
  from there. Run `drush cr` after editing.
#}
{# link_attributes arrives as a plain array, and only `attributes` is turned
   into an Attribute for you -- so build this one, defaulting it so a
   standalone preview of the component still renders. #}
{% set link = create_attribute(link_attributes ?? {}) %}
<div{{ attributes.addClass('cart-block').setAttribute('data-neo-cart', variation) }}>
  {# addClass takes ONE array; extra arguments are silently dropped. #}
  <a{{ link.addClass(['cart-block--link', 'flex', 'items-center', 'gap-2']) }}>
    {% if display == 'badge' %}
      {# The badge overhangs the icon, so the icon needs to be the positioning
         context. `badge` is a neo_base utility and carries shape only — the
         colour is ours to pick, the same way neo_toolbar does it. #}
      <span class="cart-block--icon relative inline-flex shrink-0 text-lg">
        {{ icon }}
        {% if count > 0 %}
          <span class="cart-block--badge badge absolute -top-1 -right-2 bg-primary-500 text-primary-500-content" aria-hidden="true">{{ count }}</span>
        {% endif %}
      </span>
      {# The badge reads as a bare "3", which announces nothing on its own, so
         the real sentence is kept for screen readers. #}
      <span class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">{{ count_text }}</span>
    {% else %}
      {% if icon %}
        <span class="cart-block--icon shrink-0 text-lg">{{ icon }}</span>
      {% endif %}
      <span
        class="cart-block--count"
        aria-live="polite"
        aria-atomic="true"
      >{{ count_text }}</span>
    {% endif %}
  </a>
  {% if show_dropdown and content %}
    <div class="cart-block--contents">{{ content }}</div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
